{"name":"Black Stallion","hex":"#0e191c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"stallion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male horse.\nSpecifically, one that is uncastrated.\nA male horse kept primarily as a stud.","Specifically, one that is uncastrated."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stallion"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Black Stallion","blocks":[{"text":"The Black Stallion is a series of novels by Walter Farley, beginning with the book of the same name published in 1941. The title character, an Arab stallion also known as the Black, is a sheikh’s prized stallion who comes into possession of one Alec Ramsay. Later books in the series furnish the Black's backstory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_stallion_1st_edition_cover.jpg/330px-Black_stallion_1st_edition_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Black_Stallion","wikidata":"Q884454"},{"title":"The Black Stallion (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Black Stallion is a 1979 American adventure film based on the 1941 classic children's novel of the same name by Walter Farley. The film starts in 1946, five years after the book was published. It tells the story of Alec Ramsey, a boy who is shipwrecked on a deserted island with a wild Arabian stallion that he befriends. After being rescued, they are set on entering a race challenging two champion horses."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Black_stallion_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Black_Stallion_(film)","wikidata":"Q2300266"},{"title":"Black Stallion (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Stallion is a 2010 Malayalam erotic action-thriller film directed by Pramod Pappan and written by Rajesh Jayaraman. The film was produced by Jagadeesh Chandran and featuring Kalabhavan Mani, Bala and Namitha play the lead roles in this film. This is Namitha's first film in Malayalam. The film received a lot of negative reviews from the audience, criticizing the film's direction, story, dialogues, music, editing, cinematography and cast performances. The film was dubbed in Tamil as Nil Gavani."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5e/Black_Stallion_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Stallion_(film)","wikidata":"Q4921893"},{"title":"Stallion","blocks":[{"text":"A stallion is an adult male horse that has not been gelded (castrated). Stallions follow the conformation and phenotype of their breed, but within that standard, the presence of hormones such as testosterone may give stallions a thicker, \"cresty\" neck, as well as a somewhat more muscular physique as compared to female horses, known as mares, and castrated males, called geldings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Puerto_rican-Paso-Fino-Horse-chestnut.jpg/330px-Puerto_rican-Paso-Fino-Horse-chestnut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stallion","wikidata":"Q757833"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Fellpony.jpg/500px-Fellpony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Fellpony.jpg/500px-Fellpony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A stallion walking","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFellpony.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/389-o-Cathael-Idris-13-WD-0.jpg/500px-389-o-Cathael-Idris-13-WD-0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/389-o-Cathael-Idris-13-WD-0.jpg/1280px-389-o-Cathael-Idris-13-WD-0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/389-o-Cathael-Idris-13-WD-0.jpg/500px-389-o-Cathael-Idris-13-WD-0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A stallion's secondary characteristics include heavier muscling than is seen in mares or geldings, often with muscular development along the crest of the neck.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A389-o-Cathael-Idris-13-WD-0.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Flehmendes_Pferd_32_c.jpg/500px-Flehmendes_Pferd_32_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Flehmendes_Pferd_32_c.jpg/1280px-Flehmendes_Pferd_32_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Flehmendes_Pferd_32_c.jpg/500px-Flehmendes_Pferd_32_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stallion exhibiting the flehmen response","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlehmendes_Pferd_32_c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/The_comparative_anatomy_of_the_domesticated_animals_%281873%29_%2820669607015%29.jpg/500px-The_comparative_anatomy_of_the_domesticated_animals_%281873%29_%2820669607015%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.o